---
config: tests/fresco_sessions.config
args: --fresco --path=lib/stdlib
---

CP unquotes retain ordinary result types
<| {42} |>
stdout : 42 : Int

CP composition exchanges values and returns the caller result
examples/sessions/gng-cp.links
filemode : true
stdout : 13 : Int

CP selection and offer execute the calculator
examples/sessions/calc-cp-endbang.links
filemode : true
stdout : 42 : Int

CP linking executes in both orientations
examples/sessions/fuse-cp.links
filemode : true
stdout : (42, 42) : (Int, Int)

CP composition closes the split sending endpoint
<| nu c.(c[] | c().{42}) |>
stdout : 42 : Int

CP give checks the payload before rebinding the channel
<| nu c.(c[40+2].c[] | c(x).c().{x}) |>
stdout : 42 : Int

CP composition requires a split sending end on the left
<| nu c.({close(c)} | {close(c)}) |>
exit : 1
stderr : @.*Type error:.*

CP give-nothing requires a split sending end
fun(c:End) { <| c[] |> }
exit : 1
stderr : @.*Type error:.*

CP channel endpoints cannot be duplicated
fun(c:(!().End)) { (<| c[] |>,c) }
exit : 1
stderr : @.*Type error:.*

CP spawned code cannot capture a contextual function
{ var f = fun() { 42 }; <| nu c.(c[f()].c[] | c(x).c().{x}) |> }
exit : 1
stderr : @.*Type error:.*

CP composition rejects the caller's handled effect in its child
effect E { Read : () => Int; } handle <E> (<| nu c.(c[do Read].c[] | c(x).c().{x}) |>) { case x -> x case <Read => k> -> k(42) }
exit : 1
stderr : @.*Type error:.*

CP caller code retains its handled effect
effect E { Read : () => Int; } handle <E> (<| nu c.(c[40].c[] | c(x).c().{x+do Read}) |>) { case x -> x case <Read => k> -> k(2) }
stdout : 42 : Int

CP generated primitives resist source shadowing
{ var send=0; var new=0; var accept=0; var request=0; var close=0; var wait=0; var closeBang=0; <| nu c.(c[42].c[] | c(x).c().{x}) |> }
stdout : 42 : Int

CP unquotes retain the Wild requirement
sig f : () -> Int fun f() { <| {42} |> } f()
exit : 1
stderr : @.*Type error:.*

CP payload effects run once before the channel continuation
<| nu c.(c[{ print("first"); 40 }].c[{ print("second"); 2 }].c[] | c(x).c(y).c().{x+y}) |>
stdout : firstsecond42 : Int

CP left composition consumes an absolute linear capture once
{ var f = (linfun() { 42 } : modal [] (() -@ Int)); <| nu c.(c[f()].c[] | c(x).c().{x}) |> }
stdout : 42 : Int

CP left composition rejects reuse of a linear capture
{ var f = (linfun() { 21 } : modal [] (() -@ Int)); <| nu c.(c[f()+f()].c[] | c(x).c().{x}) |> }
exit : 1
stderr : @.*Type error:.*

CP unquotes honour the split-end setting
<| {42} |>
args : --fresco --set=endbang_antiquotes=true
exit : 1
stderr : @.*Type error:.*

CP unquotes accept a split end with the setting enabled
open import FrescoPrelude; closeBang(<| {makeEndBang()} |>)
args : --fresco --path=lib/stdlib --set=endbang_antiquotes=true
stdout : () : ()

CP nested selection preserves each continuation
<| nu c.(offer c { case Go -> offer c { case Next -> c[42].c[] } } | Go c.Next c.c(x).c().{x}) |>
stdout : 42 : Int

CP consumed channel names cannot be reused
fun(c:(?().End)) { <| c().{c} |> }
exit : 1
stderr : @.*Type error:.*

CP offer rejects an empty case set
fun(c:([&|Go:!().End|&])) { <| offer c {} |> }
exit : 1
stderr : @.*Type error:.*
